# Walkthrough - Removing Browser Alerts

The application has been upgraded to replace all native browser dialogs (`alert`, [confirm](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/lib/uiStore.ts#60-78), [prompt](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/lib/uiStore.ts#79-99)) with a premium, integrated UI feedback system. This ensures a consistent and modern user experience throughout CraftCanvas.

## Changes

### 1. In-App UI Infrastructure
- **[uiStore.ts](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/lib/uiStore.ts)**: Created a centralized Zustand store to manage toasts and global dialogs.
- **[Toaster.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/ui/Toaster.tsx)**: A new component for elegant, animated toast notifications with support for Success, Error, Warning, and Info states.
- **[GlobalDialog.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/ui/GlobalDialog.tsx)**: A flexible modal system that handles confirmation requests and user prompts with custom inputs.
- **[ClientLayout.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/ClientLayout.tsx)**: Integrated the [Toaster](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/ui/Toaster.tsx#23-59) and [GlobalDialog](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/ui/GlobalDialog.tsx#8-97) into the main application structure.

### 2. Codebase Refactoring
Every instance of native browser interactions was identified and refactored:
- **Meetings**: Refactored meeting creation, deletion, and sharing flows.
- **Timetable**: Replaced native dialogs in AI planning, URL imports, and event management.
- **Daily Brief**: Updated feedback submission to use in-app prompts.
- **Tasks & Notes**: Secured deletion flows with the new confirmation modal.
- **Grades**: Modernized the data migration and component deletion experience.
- **Courses**: Integrated the new system into the Knowledge Base file management.

## Verification Results

### Automated Audit
- Ran `grep` across the entire project to ensure no `alert(`, [confirm(](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/lib/uiStore.ts#60-78), or [prompt(](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/lib/uiStore.ts#79-99) calls remain in active code.
- Verified that all new `useUIStore` calls are correctly typed and awaited where necessary.

### Visual & Interactive
- **Toasts**: Success notifications (e.g., "Link Copied") and error messages now appear as sleek, animated cards.
- **Dialogs**: Confirmation requests (e.g., "Delete Task?") now use a consistent modal design that matches the application's aesthetic.
- **Prompts**: Input requests (e.g., AI Plan title) are handled within a modern dialog interface instead of a browser-native popup.

